1 TITL United States Passport Applications, 1795-1925
1 PUBL MyHeritage
1 TEXT It is important for genealogists to note that prior to 1952 US passports were generally not required for international travel. There were only two time periods during the span of this collection when passports were required for traveling internat
2 CONC ionally: during the Civil War and World War I. Many individuals who traveled internationally will not appear on any passport index simply because passports were not required. However, passports were of particular benefit to naturalized US citizen
2 CONC s traveling abroad as the passport reduced the likelihood that their birth country would try to detain them or prevent their return to the United States.
2 CONT In addition to this passport collection, it may be beneficial to search passenger manifests. While an individual may not have needed a passport to travel internationally, they will be listed on a US citizen manifest. However, the information foun
2 CONC d on US citizen manifests is sparse compared to the information found on later passport applications.
2 CONT It was also rare for a single passport to cover multiple trips abroad. Many wealthy US citizens appear multiple times within this collection because they applied for a new passport with every voyage.
1 _TYPE Collection
1 _MEDI 10720
0 @S500040@ SOUR
1 _UPD 7 MAR 2024 19:04:36 GMT -0500 
